TEXT -192 -80 Left 3 ;1 phase example of switching off unloaded line\nwith switchback of switcher at high voltage\nbetween the poles of the switcher
TEXT -304 120 Left 3 ;At 200ms the switcher is switched off\nThe voltage at the line cap. remains from now on unchanged\nThe voltage difference between the poles rises because of \nthe changing voltage at the voltage source\nAt 650kV the switcher has a switchback at 215ms and the switcher is on\nNow the line capacitance is discharging off shortly\nwith high currents and high voltage values in the circuit \nAfter 270ms the switcher is off again\nNOTE: The transients are higher at shorter lines because of the\nhigher resonant frequencies there.
